{
  "$comment": [
    "Single machine-readable inventory of the apps in this repository. Read by",
    "scripts/manifest.mjs, which every other consumer imports: copy-dist,",
    "verify-federation-build, check-imports and the CI workflows. Before this",
    "existed the same facts were spread across `workspaces`, deploy-pages.yml,",
    "copy-dist, apps.local.json and each app's bundler config -- and two of them",
    "already disagreed about which apps get published.",
    "",
    "`bundler` gates every check that presumes the migrated shape. An app's flip",
    "to 'vite', its peerDependencies and its vite.config.ts all land in ONE",
    "commit; nothing else needs editing to bring it into scope.",
    "",
    "`configuredShared` records the POST-migration share block (what the app's",
    "vite.config.ts will declare), not what its webpack.config.js declares today.",
    "It is inert while bundler is 'webpack'. network-statistics is {} on purpose:",
    "it uses neither React nor MUI, and its current webpack config sharing them is",
    "one of the defects this migration fixes.",
    "",
    "See design/specifications/vite-migration/vite-migration.md section 8."
  ],
  "apps": [
    {
      "workspaceDir": "hello-world",
      "publishPath": "hello-world",
      "federationName": "hello",
      "port": 2222,
      "bundler": "webpack",
      "published": true,
      "exposes": ["./AppConfig", "./NetworkSummaryMenuItem"],
      "configuredShared": {
        "react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "react-dom": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "@mui/material": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^5.18.0"
        },
        "@emotion/react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^11.10.4"
        },
        "@emotion/styled": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^11.10.4"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "workspaceDir": "network-statistics",
      "publishPath": "network-statistics",
      "federationName": "networkStatistics",
      "port": 3333,
      "bundler": "webpack",
      "published": true,
      "exposes": ["./AppConfig"],
      "configuredShared": {}
    },
    {
      "workspaceDir": "network-workflows",
      "publishPath": "network-workflows",
      "federationName": "networkWorkflows",
      "port": 7000,
      "bundler": "webpack",
      "published": true,
      "exposes": ["./AppConfig"],
      "configuredShared": {
        "react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "react-dom": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "@mui/material": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^5.18.0"
        },
        "@emotion/react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^11.10.4"
        },
        "@emotion/styled": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^11.10.4"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "workspaceDir": "project-template",
      "publishPath": "project-template",
      "federationName": "template",
      "port": 5555,
      "bundler": "webpack",
      "published": true,
      "exposes": ["./AppConfig"],
      "configuredShared": {
        "react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "react-dom": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^18.3.1"
        },
        "@mui/material": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
          "requiredVersion": "^5.18.0"
        },
        "@emotion/react": {
          "singleton": true,
          "import": false,
